# PLACEHOLDER, not a real cosign public key.
#
# deploy.sh refuses to deploy until this file holds a real cosign public key that matches
# COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY (ADR-018, docs/runbooks/provision-host.md section "Image signing"). That is
# deliberate: a placeholder must fail closed, never verify anything.
#
# The owner generates the real pair once, on a machine that is not this repository's CI (the
# private key must never be committed or pasted into a chat session):
#
#   cosign generate-key-pair
#
# This writes cosign.key (password protected) and cosign.pub in the current directory. Then:
#
#   1. Replace this file with the generated cosign.pub, committed as deploy/cosign.pub.
#   2. Add repository secrets COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY (the full contents of cosign.key) and
#      COSIGN_PASSWORD (the password chosen at generation) so deploy.yml's build job can sign
#      each pushed image.
#   3. Delete the local cosign.key once the secret is stored; keep the password in the team's
#      secret manager, not in this repository.
